  "file-menu-render-bug: the File-tab click alone paints NOTHING (.pdf-file-menu-panel stayed display:none); the panel only renders on the next App-observer re-render, which this census triggers with real keystrokes into the document body (an edit flips pdfStore.isModified, which the App root observer reads). The Viewport that owns the panel does not observe isFileMenuOpen/activeFileMenuPanel — the pdf twin of the documented word/sheet File-menu bug. Every dialog pane below is censused through that side channel, one fresh page per entry, because no second re-render exists to paint a pane switch",
  "file-menu-no-close: a real click on the now-visible Back entry flips isFileMenuOpen in the store but the panel STAYS painted (block) — the same missing-observer re-render that made the File-tab click paint nothing also makes the menu impossible to close for the user",
  "file-menu-dead-entries: 2 dialog-declaring entries reach no dialog surface (Save Copy as...[menu stayed open but the entry activated no pane and no <dialog> — a dialog-declaring entry whose pane this build never renders], Rename...[menu stayed open but the entry activated no pane and no <dialog> — a dialog-declaring entry whose pane this build never renders]) — they either close the menu (non-pane action) or declare a pane the build never renders (the pdf FileMenu ships no save-copy/rename pane at all)",
  "file-menu-panes-never-paint: 6 dialog panes ACTIVATE but never paint — their pane box is statically display:none (panelBox in the pdf FileMenu), so the pane is w=0/h=0 and no real click can reach it: New...→Create New, Download as...→Download as, Print→Print Preview, Document Info...→Document Info, Advanced Settings...→Advanced Settings, Help...→Help. The census enumerates each pane's shipped controls from the DOM it mounts and fires them with SYNTHETIC domDrill clicks (none portals a real <dialog>), but only the portaled ExportWizard <dialog> (1 surface painted) is actually clickable by a user",
  "file-menu-dialog-no-dismiss: Export Wizard... — the dialog's own ✕ flips activeFileMenuPanel in the store but the dialog stays open (same missing-observer re-render), so the modal cannot be closed by the user",
  "toggle-without-overlay: 5 controls flip their own active/pressed state but open nothing (left-menu/Search, left-menu/Comments, left-menu/Navigation, left-menu/About, statusbar/Hand Tool)",
